    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling outing today, led by the elite efficiency of **Gunnar Henderson** (80.62) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27). **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a favorable matchup against the right-handed George Kirby, whose slow delivery provides the specific environment we crave for stolen base attempts. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** is a focal point against the hittable Brady Singer, bolstered by favorable wind conditions and a premium spot in the order. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (61.56) faces a stiff challenge against a high-skill arm in Jesus Luzardo, his inherent base talent and leadoff placement maintain his viability as a strong daily starter.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup today involved the bench, specifically **Curtis Mead** (48.39), who was the first cut from the starting nine. While **Curtis Mead** offered a respectable floor against Robbie Ray, the optimizer ultimately pivoted toward the defensive and positional versatility of our utility options to maintain overall 5x5 balance. We are tracking several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses, which introduces minor risk to the calculated projections for **Liam Hicks**, **Nolan Schanuel**, and others. **Josh Jung** (60.24) remains a must-start, as his baseline projection is meaningfully elevated by a 5% wind-out advantage and a clean matchup against Seth Lugo. While **Kyle Tucker** (64.73) and **Andy Pages** (59.82) are locked in for their high-upside profiles, we are monitoring the weather report closely, as any shift in wind velocity in their respective parks could necessitate a late-cycle roster adjustment.",
